  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the text overlay as the target of accusation",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the text 'looking for attention?' which frames the viewer as the one who is being accused of seeking attention. The text 'join us' further implies the user is being invited to join the group being criticized, thus projecting the user onto the scene as a potential participant in the stereotyped behavior. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but is implied through the accusatory tone and the invitation to join, which positions the viewer as the one being addressed or targeted by the meme's message.",
